  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: da92e5e775aea304a8dd2af2f973a915, type: 3}
  m_Name: dialogue_presentation_showcase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: JRPG.Data::JRPG.Data.DialogueGraphData
  id: dialogue_presentation_showcase
  displayName: Presentation Showcase
  description: Walks every dialogue importance level. Sample/regression content.
  entryNodeId: n_normal
  defaultImportance: 2
  nodes:
  - nodeId: n_normal
    speakerRef: character:char_hero
    text: This is a Normal line. It types itself out at the profile's speed, and
      the name plate above sits across the top edge of this box.
    importance: 1
    onEnterCommands: []
    onExitCommands: []
    nextNodeId: n_critical
    choices: []
    endGraphAfterThisNode: 0
    exitResolution:
      exitType: 0
      targetId: 
  - nodeId: n_critical
    speakerRef: character:char_hero
    text: "This is a Critical line. It is framed, it reveals more slowly, and it
      cannot be skipped or fast-forwarded \u2014 the frame is the tell."
    importance: 3
    onEnterCommands: []
    onExitCommands: []
    nextNodeId: n_tutorial
    choices: []
    endGraphAfterThisNode: 0
    exitResolution:
      exitType: 0
      targetId: 
  - nodeId: n_tutorial
    speakerRef: system
    text: This is a Tutorial notice. It takes the notice card over a dimmed backdrop
      rather than the conversation box, because it is instruction, not dialogue.
    importance: 4
    onEnterCommands: []
    onExitCommands: []
    nextNodeId: n_system
    choices: []
    endGraphAfterThisNode: 0
    exitResolution:
      exitType: 0
      targetId: 
  - nodeId: n_system
    speakerRef: system
    text: This is a System notice. Same card treatment as Tutorial, different accent.
    importance: 5
    onEnterCommands: []
    onExitCommands: []
    nextNodeId: n_choices
    choices: []
    endGraphAfterThisNode: 0
    exitResolution:
      exitType: 0
      targetId: 
  - nodeId: n_choices
    speakerRef: character:char_hero
    text: And this is a choice node. The stack is its own surface, not inline in
      the body. Two of these are gated, and each says why.
    importance: 2
    onEnterCommands: []
    onExitCommands: []
    nextNodeId: 
    choices:
    - choiceId: c_ok
      displayText: That all rendered correctly.
      nextNodeId: n_done
      conditions: []
      commands: []
    - choiceId: c_needs_item
      displayText: Hand over the relic.
      nextNodeId: n_done
      conditions:
      - type: 2
        stringA: equip_test_ward_ring
        stringB: 
        intA: 4
        boolA: 0
      commands: []
    - choiceId: c_needs_level
      displayText: Overpower them.
      nextNodeId: n_done
      conditions:
